<title>ESTONIA: THREE COMPANIES SEEK BOURSE MEMBERSHIP.</title>
<headline>THREE COMPANIES SEEK BOURSE MEMBERSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tallinn stock exchange said on Thursday that its board will discuss applications by three companies to become bourse members on Friday.</p>
<p>Managing director Helo Meigas told Reuters that the companies are Beeta Invest, Krediidipank and NG Kapital, a subsidiary of Norma group.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
